[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 7 port for the Huawei Y210, based on the legacy Qualcomm MSM7x27A/MSM7K-era stack. The current focus is real device stability and compatibility with the stock Y210 behaviour, especially graphics, gralloc/copybit/framebuffer, audio, radio, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and camera bring-up.

[B]Device specs[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Device: Huawei Y210
[*]Android version: 2.3.7 Gingerbread (CyanogenMod 7)
[*]SoC family: Qualcomm MSM7x27A / MSM7K-era
[*]GPU: Adreno 200
[*]Framebuffer: 320x480, ARGB8888 (32 bpp)
[*]HAL style: legacy Qualcomm/Android 2.3 stack
[*]FM chip: WCN2243 (I2S digital output to MSM7x27A codec)
[/LIST]

[B]Current status — Stable[/B]

Build: [B]cm-7-20261020-UNOFFICIAL-y210.zip[/B] | MD5: 9c4d21e5846796d4a511fc3707a6551b

[COLOR="Red"][B]Read before flashing:[/B][/COLOR] please read the known issues before flashing.

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Boot & system:[/B] boots to launcher after a clean flash/wipe
[*][B]SurfaceFlinger / mediaserver:[/B] stay alive in the current graphics path
[*][B]Display / framebuffer:[/B] gralloc.y210 and copybit.y210 load without crashing the UI; 320x480 ARGB8888 framebuffer; asynchronous framebuffer posting like stock (eglSwapBuffers ~29.5 ms -> ~3 ms)
[*][B]HW acceleration:[/B] Adreno 200 path active; SurfaceFlinger reports Adreno renderer; stride bug corrected (no horizontal repetition)
[*][B]UI / launcher:[/B] usable on-device; status bar renders correctly (ghost/duplication fixed)
[*][B]Touchscreen:[/B] single-touch and multitouch input; physical and capacitive buttons
[*][B]Backlight / LED / vibrator:[/B] screen backlight, notification LED and vibrator work
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] enables, scans, associates and obtains DHCP; on/off cycles; [B]keeps working after deep sleep[/B] (the stock ROM loses the data path after sleeping until Wi-Fi is toggled; fixed in the kernel). The Atheros AR6003 driver is now built from source and applies Huawei's per-unit TX power calibration like stock
[*][B]Wi-Fi hotspot:[/B] clients connect, get an address and browse over mobile data; Wi-Fi reconnects on its own when the hotspot is turned off
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] pairing, file transfer (Object Push) and A2DP audio validated with real hardware (2026-07 build)
[*][B]Telephony / RIL:[/B] baseband, operator registration, signal, IMEI, calls (incoming/outgoing, earpiece and speaker, mute), SMS and HSPA mobile data; [B]SIM is now detected as READY[/B]: IMSI, operator numeric and SPN read from the SIM, APN list works in Settings; [B]SIM PIN lock[/B]: PIN prompt at boot, enabling/disabling the lock and changing the PIN
[*][B]Sensors / rotation:[/B] accelerometer, gravity and linear-accel sensors work with stock sensors.default.so; /dev/accel permissions corrected
[*][B]ADB / logs:[/B] adb logcat and runtime logging are usable
[*][B]Audio playback:[/B] AudioFlinger -> libaudio output works
[*][B]Audio recording:[/B] SoundRecorder / voice recorder works
[*][B]FM radio:[/B] real tuning and real audio of the station through headphones and speaker, manual tuning, [B]seek up and seek down[/B]
[*][B]Camera app:[/B] opens consistently with the current libcamera wrapper
[*][B]Camera:[/B] 640x480 colour portrait preview, JPEG photo capture at full 2MP (1600x1200), close -> reopen, photo/video switch (fixed preview freeze), H.263 352x288 15 fps video recording (MP4 in gallery)
[*][B]Video playback:[/B] compatible files play; H.264 Baseline was tested
[*][B]Storage / USB:[/B] /data, SD card and USB mass storage
[*][B]Suspend / screen off / deep sleep:[/B] continuous deep sleep validated with Wi-Fi associated (Wi-Fi stays in normal 802.11 power save and is still connected on wake; only the normal modem wakeup remains)
[*][B]GPS:[/B] real satellite fix validated outdoors (up to 9 satellites, stable coordinates); raw NMEA sentences for apps that read them; correct location dates
[*][B]Performance profile:[/B] interactive CPU governor, noop I/O scheduler on NAND, tuned lowmemorykiller profile, 48 MB zram swap (no lowmemorykiller kills under heavy multitasking) and preoptimized (dexpreopt) framework and apps
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]HD video (640x480 H.264):[/B] not supported — this Y210 revision has no hardware video encoder for that resolution
[*][B]First boot warning:[/B] com.android.provision may log a non-blocking WindowManager InflateException while creating the starting window after wipe
[*][B]FM seek:[/B] stops only on stations the FM chip can detect; across a stretch of band with none it takes as long as a full sweep (about 70 ms per 100 kHz), and reception depends on the headphone cable (it is the antenna)
[*][B]Not re-tested on this build yet:[/B] Bluetooth A2DP (worked on the 2026-07 build)
[/LIST]

