[SIZE="4"][B]Changelog:[/B][/SIZE]

[B]2026-10-20[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Wi-Fi hotspot fixed:[/B] it did not start on the 2026-10-18 build. The Wi-Fi client library refused to talk to the hotspot daemon while the normal Wi-Fi service was stopped (which it always is in hotspot mode), and a leftover control socket from a previous run made the next start fail. Turning the hotspot off now brings normal Wi-Fi back on its own
[*][B]Wi-Fi driver built from source:[/B] the Atheros AR6003 driver now comes from the AR6kSDK 3.1 sources instead of Huawei's binary, and includes Huawei's per-unit TX power calibration (read from the phone's own calibration file, as stock does)
[*][B]SIM PIN:[/B] entering the PIN at boot always said "wrong PIN" (the request never reached the SIM, so no attempts were used); fixed. The "SIM network unlock PIN" screen that briefly appeared after a correct PIN is gone. Enabling/disabling the lock and changing the PIN work
[*][B]GPS:[/B] raw NMEA sentences ($GPGGA, $GPRMC, $GPGSV...) now reach apps; the modem firmware predates the 2019 GPS week rollover and dated everything 1024 weeks in the past (2007), now corrected in location times and in the NMEA dates
[*][B]FM seek down works:[/B] the FM chip firmware sweeps the band without stopping when seeking down (Huawei's own FM software sends the same command); the kernel driver now emulates it with upward seeks
[*][B]FM seek is much faster:[/B] the signal threshold was being sent as an out-of-range value, so the chip only stopped on very strong stations and the app gave up after 5 s; seeks now take about 0.5-3 s when there are stations nearby
[*][B]FM without headphones:[/B] opening the radio without headphones no longer crashes the app or leaves the radio stuck after plugging them in; it now just asks for headphones
[*][B]Kernel:[/B] updated to commit 8efe2f16 (FM seek down)
[/LIST]

[B]2026-10-18[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Kernel:[/B] the ROM now ships a kernel built from source ([URL="https://github.com/chijure/android_kernel_huawei_y210"]android_kernel_huawei_y210[/URL]) instead of the stock Huawei binary. Same errors and behaviour as stock, plus:
[LIST]
[*]Kernel boot time 6.6 s -> 3.5 s: it no longer probes ten camera sensors and several chips the Y210 does not have (only the real mt9d113 camera sensor is built)
[*]Fixed Wi-Fi losing its data path after deep sleep (also present on stock): the Wi-Fi SDIO slot is no longer re-initialized on resume
[*]zram and swap support
[*]About 150 fewer error lines in dmesg at boot (I2C NACKs from probing absent chips are now debug-level)
[/LIST]
[*][B]RIL:[/B] the SIM was always reported as UNKNOWN because the stock RIL library speaks the newer v6 RIL API; a small translation layer now converts SIM status, IMSI, SIM I/O and data-call replies. SIM state, IMSI, operator and SPN now come from the SIM, and the APN list in Settings works without workarounds
[*][B]Memory:[/B] 48 MB zram swap: under heavy multitasking no apps or services are killed by lowmemorykiller (3 kills before) and more file cache is kept
[*][B]Dexpreopt:[/B] framework and apps are preoptimized at build time: 28 MB more free space on /data and a quick first boot after flashing or wiping dalvik
[*][B]Graphics:[/B] asynchronous framebuffer posting like stock (eglSwapBuffers ~29.5 ms -> ~3 ms); several copybit fixes (video and camera preview blits, preview chroma)
[*][B]Performance:[/B] CheckJNI disabled like on stock (faster app launch)
[*][B]FM:[/B] seek now uses the standard V4L2 seek call; seek up works
[*][B]Media:[/B] camera videos (.m4v) are now indexed by the media scanner; fixed thumbnails failing for about half of the PNG images
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] uses the standard CM7 Wi-Fi HAL; driver load waits for the firmware before starting the supplicant
[*][B]Claro Peru APNs[/B] included
[*]Internal: almost all Y210-specific changes now live in the device tree instead of patches over the CM7 source (21 -> 11 patches)
[/LIST]

[B]2026-07-12[/B]
[LIST]
[*]FM radio: real audio finally fixed — the missing piece was opening /dev/msm_fm and starting an audmgr session before the audio routing RPC, matching real hardware behaviour
[*]FM volume: fixed a bug where lowering the slider never actually muted, and a second bug where most of the lower/middle range of the slider had no audible effect
[*]Several internal audio HAL stability fixes (uninitialized variables, a broken CSV parser branch, a TTY mode flag that could get silently reset)
[*]Fixed a pre-existing bug where switching between photo and video mode left the preview frozen (a leftover "keep hardware alive" workaround was reusing a stale camera buffer handle)
[*]Camera: photo capture now uses the sensor's real 2MP resolution (1600x1200) instead of being capped at VGA
[*]Status bar: fixed a grey strip on the left of the expanded panel and the date drawing on top of the notification icons
[*]Fixed the same nine-patch background defect (a degenerate 1px stretch region) across every title-bar-style background in the tree, including PackageInstaller
[*]Performance: found and fixed the CPU tuning script never being packaged into the build at all, so the Y210 CPU profile was silently never applied on a fresh flash
[*]Performance: switched the CPU governor from ondemand to interactive (already built into the kernel, unused), switched the NAND I/O scheduler from cfq to noop, and lowered the dirty-page writeback threshold — all verified on real hardware
[/LIST]

[B]2026-07-10[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Clean flash from scratch validated end-to-end (no manual staging): 54/54 automated checks passed
[*]Bluetooth A2DP audio validated with real headphones
[*]GPS real satellite fix validated outdoors
[*]Diagnosed low headset volume as a physical/dirty jack issue on the test unit, not software
[/LIST]

[B]2026-07-09[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Voice calls: uplink/microphone confirmed working on a real call
[*]Bluetooth: pairing and file transfer confirmed working with real hardware
[*]Kernel: removed a leftover FPGA-only register write that ran on every FM power-up on real hardware (reference-board code path, harmless but incorrect)
[*]FM: fixed event delivery from the kernel driver to the app (was silently stuck in a loop, never received real tune/RSSI events)
[/LIST]

[B]2026-07-06[/B]
[LIST]
[*]FM radio: real RF tuning confirmed (genuine RSSI and tune events, not simulated)
[*]FM radio: firmware no longer gets wiped on a second open of the tuner device
[/LIST]

[B]2026-06-13[/B]
[LIST]
[*]FM radio: patched tavarua kernel driver to skip hardware re-init when firmware is already loaded, preventing firmware loss on second open of /dev/radio0; audio validation pending
[/LIST]

[B]2026-06-12[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Clean flash validated: first boot completes, PackageManager rebuilds state, launcher starts
[*]Graphics path stable enough for launcher use; gralloc.y210/copybit.y210 no longer collapse the UI
[*]Adreno 200 renderer active in SurfaceFlinger
[*]Wi-Fi validated: enable, scan, associate, DHCP
[*]Bluetooth enables through restored QCOM route
[*]Audio playback and audio recording validated
[*]Camera app opens consistently; 640x480 preview remains stable on first open; video recording validated (H.263 352x288 15 fps → MP4)
[*]Y210 CPU governor and lowmemorykiller runtime profile restored
[*]Accelerometer /dev/accel permissions corrected (chmod 0664 in init.y210.rc was missing indentation and being silently ignored)
[/LIST]

[B]2026-05-24[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed Adreno 200 horizontal stride bug: gralloc forced to single-buffer so EGL receives a PMEM fd instead of the framebuffer fd, giving correct 320 px stride (was 128 px, causing 2.5x image repetition)
[*]Fixed framebuffer copy path to use memcpy instead of MSMFB_BLIT for PMEM sub-heap fds
[*]Fixed FD_CLOEXEC on all persistent audio file descriptors to prevent EBUSY on /dev/msm_pcm_out after fork
[*]Reverted headset post-processing mask from "full" to "lite" (EQ+IIR, no MBADRC) — MBADRC was compressing the DSP output and nullifying the software volume control
[*]Fixed missing keymap: default_keypad.kcm and all keylayout .kl files added to device tree
[*]Fixed ringtone/notification props to use files that exist in CM7 (Huawei_Tune.ogg / Glory.ogg do not exist)
[*]Added HSDPA/HSPA TCP buffer sizes to init.y210.rc
[/LIST]

[B]2026-05-23[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed gralloc.msm7k.so contamination: clean rebuild of libgralloc-qsd8k with Android.mk guards; previous binary had symbols from both gralloc modules causing a bootloop
[/LIST]

[B]2026-05-22[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed status bar ghost/duplication: StatusBarManagerService now skips redundant propagation to mBar when icon state did not change
[*]Fixed RIL double-poll: removed redundant notifyRegistrants() call on events 1033/1037 (DATA_NETWORK_STATE_CHANGED), which was causing rapid signal icon flicker
[*]Fixed page-flip detection in gralloc framebuffer: yres_virtual check corrected; refresh rate guard changed from == 0 to < 1 Hz to correctly detect the Y210 pixel clock
[/LIST]

